## Working Principle

1. The soil moisture sensor measures the moisture condition of the soil.
2. NodeMCU reads the analog sensor value.
3. The sensor value is converted into an approximate moisture percentage.
4. If the moisture level falls below the lower threshold, the pump is activated.
5. When sufficient moisture is reached, the pump is switched off.
6. Wi-Fi connectivity provides the foundation for sending system information to Firebase.

## Automatic Control Logic

| Soil Moisture | Pump Action             |
| ------------- | ----------------------- |
| Below 35%     | Pump ON                 |
| 35–54%        | Maintain previous state |
| 55% or above  | Pump OFF                |

Two different thresholds are used to reduce unnecessary rapid switching of the relay.

## Sensor Calibration

The system uses configurable dry and wet sensor reference values:

```cpp
const int dryValue = 850;
const int wetValue = 350;
```

These values should be calibrated according to the actual sensor and environmental conditions.

## Pin Configuration

